<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Siege</p><h1 class="enc-title">Siege of Fort Neoheroka</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1713">1713</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tuscarora-war">Tuscarora War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Siege of Fort Neoheroka was the decisive action of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tuscarora-war">Tuscarora War</a> in North Carolina. In March 1713 a colonial force under Colonel James Moore of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-carolina">South Carolina</a>, made up mostly of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yamasee">Yamasee</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cherokee">Cherokee</a> and other Native allies, besieged the fortified Tuscarora town of Neoheroka and destroyed it with fire. Hundreds of Tuscarora were killed and hundreds more captured and sold as slaves, and many survivors moved north to join the Iroquois.</p></div>
